 "notes": [
  "The desk is the same premium-dealer-build app for every dealer, so the shots, actions, demo data and css are house values: change none of them per client. Only the clock (DESK_CLOCK: the day the off-camera deal's documents are signed, 14:00 local, = partB.clock in client-inputs.json, else clock) and the timezone are filled.",
  "Running order and why: SKILL.md 'Part B: the desk'. Every constant: references/house-recipe.md §16. Problems and fixes: references/lessons.md, part B. Gates and stills: references/verification.md, part B.",
  "Capture order on ONE fresh desk server (next dev on :5190, DESK_PREVIEW_MEMBER=fresh, nextjs-portal hidden by css): 6-desk-signin, 7-desk-onboard (onboards Maria Lopez on camera: her strokes are the saved signature on every later document), 8-desk-sale-start, 9-desk-buyer, then the B4 set-up deal (desk-walk sale.cjs with scenarios/james-carter-to-registration.json copy) and 11-desk-guide --var deal=<it>, then 10-desk-readback (makes its own deal), then the off-camera complete sale (sale.cjs james-carter.json + ceremony.cjs) and 12-desk-signed --var deal=<it>. Restart the server before re-capturing 6 or 7.",
  "After capture, measure partB.cuts on the captures (verification.md, part B) and fill client-inputs.json → partB; pdftoppm -r 300 the deal's 130-U page 1 into public/docs/130u-p1.png."
 ],
